    "title": "N.M. legislators tackle funding for WIPP road repair",
    "summary": "Just before the end of the federal government’s 2026 fiscal year, members of New Mexico’s congressional delegation announced $10 million in funding to repair roads used to transport waste to the Waste Isolation Pilot Plant, near Carlsbad, N.M. Press releases from Sen. Ben Ray Luján and Rep. Gabe Vasquez on September 29 followed an initial announcement from Sen. Martin Heinrich on September 28. All three legislators celebrated the funding, which Heinrich explained had initially been awarded in January through federal appropriations bills and was the first such funding to be awarded for WIPP-related road maintenance since 2014.",
